{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Python 3 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Python 3 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nThis is the easy version of the problem. The only difference between the easy version and the hard version is the constraints on $$$n$$$. You can only make hacks if both versions are solved.A permutation of $$$1, 2, \\ldots, n$$$ is a sequence of $$$n$$$ integers, where each integer from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ appears exactly once. For example, $$$[2,3,1,4]$$$ is a permutation of $$$1, 2, 3, 4$$$, but $$$[1,4,2,2]$$$ isn't because $$$2$$$ appears twice in it.Recall that the number of inversions in a permutation $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ is the number of pairs of indices $$$(i, j)$$$ such that $$$i &lt; j$$$ and $$$a_i &gt; a_j$$$.Let $$$p$$$ and $$$q$$$ be two permutations of $$$1, 2, \\ldots, n$$$. Find the number of permutation pairs $$$(p,q)$$$ that satisfy the following conditions:  $$$p$$$ is lexicographically smaller than $$$q$$$.  the number of inversions in $$$p$$$ is greater than the number of inversions in $$$q$$$. Print the number of such pairs modulo $$$mod$$$. Note that $$$mod$$$ may not be a prime.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Python 3 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\r\nfrom math import factorial\r\n\r\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\r\n\r\ntotal = 0\r\ndd = dict()\r\nqwe = set()\r\n\r\ndef stup(a, was, i, n, ans):\r\n\tif i == n:\r\n\t\tzz = 0\r\n\t\tfor i in range(n):\r\n\t\t\tfor j in range(i):\r\n\t\t\t\tif a[j] > a[i]:\r\n\t\t\t\t\tzz += 1\r\n\t\tprint(a, zz)\r\n\t\tans[zz] += 1\r\n\t\treturn\r\n\tfor v in range(n):\r\n\t\tif not was[v]:\r\n\t\t\twas[v] = True\r\n\t\t\ta[i] = v\r\n\t\t\tstup(a, was, i+1, n, ans)\r\n\t\t\twas[v] = False\r\n\r\nzz, mod = map(int, input().split())\r\nif zz == 1:\r\n\tprint(0)\r\n\texit(0)\r\n#ans = [0]*(zz*(zz-1))\r\n#stup([0]*zz, [False]*zz, 0, zz, ans)\r\n#print(ans)\r\n\r\ndef C(n, k):\r\n\treturn factorial(n)//factorial(n-k)//factorial(k)\r\n\r\nz = [1]\r\naaa = mod-1\r\nfor i in range(2,zz):\r\n\tnz = [0]*(i*i//2)\r\n\tfor j in range(len(z)):\r\n\t\tfor k in range(i):\r\n\t\t\tif z[j] > 0:\r\n\t\t\t\t#print(i-k+j, j, i-k-1)\r\n\t\t\t\tnz[i-k-1+j] += z[j]\r\n\tfor k in range(zz):\r\n\t\tfor l in range(i+1,zz):\r\n\t\t\tfor j in range(len(z)):\r\n\t\t\t\tfor jj in range(len(z)):\r\n\t\t\t\t\tif i-k-1+j > i-l-1+jj:\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\taaa = (aaa + z[j] * z[jj] * C(zz,i)) % mod\r\n\t#print(nz)\r\n\tz = nz\r\n#print(z)\r\nprint(aaa % mod)\r\nexit(0)\r\ndef solve():\r\n\tpass\r\n\r\nsolve()\r\n\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport sys\n\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ndef count_inversions(arr):\n    n = len(arr)\n    inv = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                inv += 1\n    return inv\n\ndef generate_permutations(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return [[]]\n    if n == 1:\n        return [[1]]\n    \n    perms = []\n    prev_perms = generate_permutations(n-1)\n    for perm in prev_perms:\n        for i in range(n):\n            new_perm = perm[:i] + [n] + perm[i:]\n            perms.append(new_perm)\n    return perms\n\ndef solve():\n    n, mod = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    if n == 1:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    # Generate all permutations\n    perms = generate_permutations(n)\n    num_perms = len(perms)\n    \n    # Count inversions for each permutation\n    inv_counts = [count_inversions(p) for p in perms]\n    \n    # Count pairs (p, q) where p < q lexicographically and inv(p) > inv(q)\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(num_perms):\n        for j in range(i+1, num_perms):\n            if inv_counts[i] > inv_counts[j]:\n                count += 1\n    \n    print(count % mod)\n\nsolve()\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.960462772236497e-07, -5.400034933700226e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.00025876989820972085, -3.302042750874534e-05, -0.5231348872184753, -0.030375661328434944, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.2649508537142538e-05, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -0.0002693767019081861, -0.001932421582750976, -0.03070160374045372, -0.04842901974916458, -0.002934794407337904, -2.4914430468925275e-05, -0.647853672504425, -9.858122211880982e-05, -0.00011336160969221964, -0.02436072565615177, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.3483953555114567e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -0.020306900143623352, -0.13926288485527039, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -7.867782187531702e-06, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -9.775113539944869e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.3132916986942291, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, -6.794906312279636e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.291525328881107e-06, -1.811964830267243e-05, -2.4437606043647975e-05, -5.6028206927